# Phase One — Broad Mobile Heichel Brainstorm

The Awtsmoos creates the viewport and every vessel inside its frame;
Awtsmoos.com must let content breathe, not let overlays bury the name.

## Mission

Repair Heichel Ikar on narrow/mobile screens as a coherent reading and navigation surface, not as a pile of independently-correct widgets. The screenshots prove multiple surfaces are competing: profile chrome, Living Path sticky orientation, groupings state, discovery, Advanced tools, and the global mobile dock.

## Every plausible failure surface

- stale browser/CDN module graph causing old loader code to survive after Chitas source changes;
- Living Path grouping injection not reaching the exact public module users receive;
- filter state or result counts computed before injected content is visible;
- `currentView` switching after content filtering, leaving groupings rendered from an earlier view;
- related branches rendered regardless of active view, creating contradictory "empty" + "explore" states;
- sticky Root bar becoming visible too early or never yielding on a short page;
- fixed Advanced platform panel competing with fixed bottom navigation;
- fixed panel z-index covering content controls and tabs;
- panel auto-open state persisted by native `<details>` or another script;
- profile cover/stats/actions occupying too much vertical space on phones;
- duplicate conceptual navigation: profile tabs plus Living Path tabs plus bottom global dock;
- insufficient bottom padding beneath fixed global nav;
- content containers using desktop min-heights or large empty-state geometry;
- search/filter controls wider/taller than necessary;
- Nearby Branches cards shown as if they are content results;
- groupings empty state displayed even when synthetic Chitas grouping exists;
- public asset cache not invalidated after JS/CSS changes;
- old legacy renderers still mounting in parallel with Living Path;
- owner controls or platform controls rendered when unnecessary;
- mobile safe-area calculations causing overlays on iPhone/Android browser chrome;
- mobile widths inheriting `position: fixed`, `inset`, or large `min-block-size` from desktop.

## Ideal outcome

At `?view=groupings&series=root` on Heichel Ikar:

- Groupings tab visibly contains `Daily Chitas · Chumash`.
- Result count says 1 result.
- No contradictory empty-state card is present.
- Nearby Branches is hidden while viewing Groupings; it belongs to Tree/Series context.
- The sticky Root navigator appears only after the primary path controls leave the viewport.
- Advanced is collapsed and inline on phones, never covering content or the global dock.
- Bottom global navigation has reserved content clearance.
- Heichel identity is compact enough that the actual study/navigation surface appears quickly.
- Opening Daily Chitas switches into its seven daily study cards without edit/drag controls.

## Architecture candidates

A. CSS-only mobile patch: fast but insufficient because Groupings count/state is wrong.
B. JS-only state repair: fixes Chitas visibility but leaves overlap and vertical congestion.
C. Separate mobile template: too divergent and expensive to maintain.
D. Unified repair: fix state propagation/cache identity, make discovery view-aware, make Advanced inline on mobile, tighten mobile layout with focused CSS.
E. Remove Advanced entirely: would hide useful functionality rather than solve composition.

Winner: D.
